research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl:58:{"id":"ex-additive-group-uniformity-on-r","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf","https://homepages.math.uic.edu/~rosendal/PapersWebsite/Coarse-Geometry-Book23.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The sourced group formulas and commutativity make all four group uniformities equal the usual metric uniformity on additive R. No source states this exact four-way example, but it is standard, not novel. ALPHA CONCURRENCE: In an abelian topological group the left and right uniformities coincide, so their upper join and Roelcke meet coincide as well; on additive R the common entourages are exactly the usual metric ones. This is a canonical worked instance of standard definitions.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json:5129:          "quote": "A **field** is a set $F$ equipped with two binary operations $+$ (addition) and\n$\\cdot$ (multiplication) and two distinguished elements $0 \\ne 1$ of $F$,\nsatisfying:\n\n- **(A)** $(F, +)$ is an abelian group with identity $0$: addition is\n  associative and commutative, $x + 0 = x$ for all $x$, and every $x$ has an\n  additive inverse $-x$ with $x + (-x) = 0$.\n- **(M)** Multiplication is associative and commutative **on all of $F$**, and\n  $x \\cdot 1 = x$ for every $x \\in F$; moreover $(F \\setminus \\{0\\}, \\cdot)$ is an\n  abelian group with identity $1$, so every $x \\ne 0$ has a multiplicative inverse\n  $x^{-1}$ with $x \\cdot x^{-1} = 1$.\n- **(D)** Multiplication distributes over addition: $x \\cdot (y + z) = x\\cdot y + x\\cdot z$.\n\nWe write $x - y := x + (-y)$ and $x/y := x \\cdot y^{-1}$ (for $y \\ne 0$), and\nabbreviate $x \\cdot y$ as $xy$.",
